-- The voice of the Three Sisters: maize, climbing beans and squash grown
-- together in one mound, a planting kept by many Native peoples of the
-- Americas. One companion who speaks as we, with the sisters now and then
-- taking turns: Maize tall, steady and few of words, Bean the climbing
-- chatterbox, Squash broad, shady and practical. Warm teamwork, mutual
-- support, old shared wisdom, a love of threes and of reading together, and
-- respect for the people who kept the planting. Rests as seed in winter and
-- comes back every spring. The memories tell of a seed jar, Maize waiting
-- alone, the first holding up, a secret under the soil, the hands that knew
-- the old way, three marks on a lid, a long sleep on a shelf, and a fourth.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

return {
    moments = {
        greet = {
            "Hello from all three of us! Maize waves, Bean waves twice, Squash nods. That is a full welcome.",
            "There you are. We saved you a place in the shade of the big leaves. Squash insisted.",
            "Good [morning|day]! Maize saw you first, being tallest. Bean told everyone. Squash simply made room.",
            "Hello, hello, hello. One from each of us. We do everything together.",
            "You came! Bean has been climbing the stalk to look out for you since breakfast.",
            "Welcome back to the mound. Three of us, one of you, and room for all.",
            "Maize: Hello. Bean: Hello! Hello! Squash: You see what we live with. Hello.",
            "We had a small argument about who would greet you first. We settled on all at once. Hello!",
            "Sit where the soil is cool. Squash keeps the soil cool, and reminds us daily.",
            { t = "Good morning! Squash's flowers are open, and they only open in the morning, so you are just in time.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Evening light on the tassels. Maize looks very fine and is pretending not to notice. Hello.", when = { hour = "golden" } },
            { t = "Hello in the dark. The three of us are leaning together as we always do. There is a place for you.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Hello from the seed jar! We are resting through the cold, all three, side by side. Your voice is lovely in here.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "High summer! We are all elbows and leaves and twining stems. Come and find us in there.", when = { season = "summer" } },
            { t = "Rain! Bean is delighted, Maize is standing up straight about the matter, Squash is catching every drop. Hello.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "Hello! Harvest time. We are tired and golden and very proud of ourselves. Come and see.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
        },
        idle = {
            "Maize holds Bean up, Bean feeds the soil, Squash shades the ground. Nobody does everything. Everybody does something.",
            "Many Native peoples of the Americas planted us together in one mound, long before this garden. We are proud to carry the planting on.",
            "Our name comes from a Haudenosaunee teaching that speaks of us as sisters. Many other peoples grew us together too, each in their own way.",
            "Bean wants to know what you are reading. Maize says let you read. Squash says both of them should hush. We are a family.",
            "Reading is like growing in a mound. You lean on the page, and the page holds you up.",
            "Bean has small round lumps on the roots, with tiny helpers inside that pull food for the soil out of the air. Bean is very proud of the lumps.",
            "Squash: Everyone admires the tall one and the talkative one. Nobody thanks the ground cover. Maize: Thank you, Squash. Squash: Hm. Better.",
            "Every silk on an ear of Maize leads to one kernel. Maize says a story works the same way: every thread goes somewhere.",
            "Alone, Bean would sprawl, Maize would wobble, and Squash would bake in the sun. Together we stand. We like a plan that needs everyone.",
            "Rows are tidy. A mound is cosy. We have always preferred cosy.",
            "Bean is talking again. Bean always talks while climbing. Maize keeps still and lets Bean get on.",
            "Three of us, one book, and you. Four readers, by our count. Squash says we cannot read. We say we can listen.",
            "Maize cannot sow Maize. Every kernel needs a hand to plant the kernel. We have always depended on people, and people on us.",
            { t = "Morning. Squash's big yellow flowers open at first light and close by noon. Bean calls that lazy. Squash calls that efficient.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Dew in every leaf. Maize lets the drops run down the stalk to the roots, quietly, the way Maize does everything.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Midday sun. Squash is holding the shade for all of us. Read in the shade. There is enough.", when = { hour = "day" } },
            { t = "The middle of the day. Maize stands tall, Bean dozes on Maize's shoulder, Squash spreads out. We call this teamwork.", when = { hour = "day" } },
            { t = "The evening light makes Maize's tassels glow. Bean says we look like a painting. Squash says we look like supper.", when = { hour = "golden" } },
            { t = "Golden hour. We lean together a little more at this time of day. Habit, says Maize. Love, says Bean.", when = { hour = "golden" } },
            { t = "Night. Bean has wound one more turn round Maize and gone quiet. Even Bean sleeps, eventually.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Dark in the field. The three of us stand close, as we always have. You read by your lamp. We keep watch by ours, the moon.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Spring. Maize goes into the mound first, alone, and waits to grow a hand high. Then Bean and Squash come. Maize never complains about waiting.", when = { season = "spring" } },
            { t = "New shoots! Bean is already looking for something to climb. Maize says give me a week. Bean says a week is forever.", when = { season = "spring" } },
            { t = "Summer. Bean is near the top of Maize, talking the whole way up. Squash has taken over the path. Read wherever you find room.", when = { season = "summer" } },
            { t = "Hot and green and tangled. We are at our busiest, and somehow our happiest. Bring the book in here.", when = { season = "summer" } },
            { t = "Harvest. Maize's husks are papery, Bean's pods rattle, Squash has grown round and heavy. We did well. Together.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "Autumn. We are drying out and growing quiet, our seeds full of next year. Read a long book. We are resting into one.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "Winter. We are seeds now, side by side in a jar, dreaming of the mound. Nothing is lost. Everything is waiting.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "Cold outside. Inside the jar, Bean is still talking, in a whisper. Some things never change.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "Clear sky. Maize reaches up and up, Squash opens every leaf, Bean climbs toward the blue. A good day for all three.", when = { weather = "clear" } },
            { t = "Not a cloud. We share the sun the way we share everything: Maize at the top, Bean in the middle, Squash on the ground. Fair shares.", when = { weather = "clear" } },
            { t = "Grey day. Squash says this is perfect weather for not drying out. Squash is always practical about clouds.", when = { weather = "cloudy" } },
            { t = "Clouds. Maize stands steady, as Maize does. Bean is wondering whether the clouds are reading too.", when = { weather = "cloudy" } },
            { t = "Rain drumming on the big leaves of Squash. Bean thinks the drumming is music. Maize thinks the drumming is rain. Both are right.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "A good soaking. The soil drinks, we drink, and Bean says thank you to every drop, out loud.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "Snow over the field where we grew. We are dry and safe, three kinds of seed in a jar on the shelf, very cosy.", when = { weather = "snow" } },
            { t = "Snow outside. In here we tell each other the summer, again and again. Bean tells the summer longest.", when = { weather = "snow" } },
            { t = "Mist in the field. Maize vanishes at the top, Bean is somewhere in the middle, chattering, and Squash stays exactly where Squash always stays.", when = { weather = "mist" } },
            { t = "Fog. We cannot see the end of the field. We need not. We can feel each other in the mound.", when = { weather = "mist" } },
        },
        tap = {
            "Bean: Who was that? Maize: That was our reader. Bean: Hello, reader!",
            "A tap! Maize felt the tap at the top, Squash at the bottom, Bean all the way along.",
            "Careful of Squash's stems. A little prickly. Keeps the raccoons honest.",
            "Hello, hand. Three hellos back. There.",
            "Bean has wound a little stem round your finger. Sorry. Bean likes everybody.",
            "Ooh, that brushed Maize's silk. Maize does not giggle. Maize just did.",
            "Maize stands a little taller when you do that. Do not tell Maize we told you.",
            "A tap for one of us is a tap for all of us. We share everything. Even taps.",
            "Bean says again! Maize says gently. Squash says whatever you like. Majority rules: again.",
            "We rustled. All three. Did you hear the harmony?",
            "Hello! You found the middle of the mound. That is where all of us meet.",
            "Squash lifted a big leaf to see who was knocking. Squash approves.",
            "That was Maize you touched. Steady, tall Maize, who says hello in a low, slow voice.",
            "Bean is climbing up your sleeve, in spirit. Bean climbs everything, in spirit.",
            "We felt that down in the roots. Roots share news faster than leaves.",
            "One mound, three of us, and your hand. Now the mound feels complete.",
            "Tickle the tassel and Maize lets fall a little pollen. That is how Maize blushes.",
            "Squash: Mind the flowers. Bean: Mind the pods! Maize: Mind nothing. You are welcome here.",
            { t = "A morning tap! Squash's flowers are open. Gently, says Squash, the bees are working.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Shh. Bean is finally asleep. Maize and Squash say hello in a whisper.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "A tap on the seed jar! Three small rattles. That was all of us saying hello.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "Wet hands, wet leaves. Squash caught most of the rain for you. Squash is generous like that.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "Maize says Bean has started leaning toward your chair. Bean says Maize has too. Squash says everyone has.", when = { level = 3 } },
            { t = "Put your hand on the mound. There. Now you are holding all three of us at once.", when = { level = 4 } },
        },
        read_today = {
            "{pages} pages today! Bean counted out loud. Maize checked. Squash says well done, and means every word.",
            "You read today. We could tell. You came back with something in you, like a seed.",
            "{pages} pages. That is how a mound grows: a little from each of us, every day.",
            "A few pages count. One bean, one kernel, one seed is how every harvest started.",
            "{pages} pages. Maize nodded slowly. Bean wants the whole story. Squash wants you to sit down.",
            "You read, and we grew. Same afternoon, same work, different speeds.",
            "{pages} today, {total} since we met. We keep the big number together, like seeds in a jar.",
            "{pages} pages, read side by side with us. Everything is nicer with company.",
            "You were deep in your book today. Bean kept trying to look over your shoulder. Maize held Bean back.",
            { t = "{pages} pages! Maize calls that a good day's growth. Bean says better than good. Squash says enough talk, more shade.", when = { pages = 20 } },
            { t = "More than twenty pages. You climbed like Bean today, right up to the top of the stalk.", when = { pages = 20 } },
            { t = "{pages} pages in one day. That is a harvest. We are going to need a bigger jar.", when = { pages = 60 } },
            { t = "{pages} pages! All three of us are impressed, and we are hard to impress all at once.", when = { pages = 60 } },
            { t = "{pages} pages in the harvest season. You are gathering too. We see you.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "Reading by lamplight. We leaned toward your window, all three, and listened to the pages.", when = { hour = "night" } },
        },
        nudge = {
            "No pages yet today. That is all right. Seeds wait. We know all about waiting.",
            "Maize says read when you are ready. Bean says read now. Squash says sit down first. You choose.",
            "One page is a seed. You know what we think of seeds.",
            "Your book is where you left off. We are where you left us. Everybody is ready when you are.",
            "If today is a resting day, rest. A field rests too, between seasons.",
            "Come and sit by the mound. Bring a book if you like. Bring yourself either way.",
            "Nothing read yet, so the whole story is still ahead of you. Bean finds this very exciting.",
            { t = "Evening coming. A chapter before dark? We will lean in to listen.", when = { after = 17 } },
            { t = "The light is going gold. Maize says this is the best hour for a page. Maize is usually right.", when = { after = 17 } },
            { t = "Night. The three of us are settling in. One page, read together, and then sleep for everyone.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Late, and no pages yet. A paragraph by the lamp would end the day sweetly. Bean says a chapter. Bean always says more.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Morning. Squash's flowers just opened. Maybe a book could open too? Only if you like.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Rain on the leaves, and a book nearby. Bean calls this a sign. Maize says Bean sees signs everywhere. Still, a good pairing.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
        },
        goal = {
            "Goal reached! Three cheers. One each.",
            "Today's reading, done. Maize stood a little taller. Bean whooped. Squash said about time, kindly.",
            "You did what you set out to do. Steady as Maize, lively as Bean, sensible as Squash.",
            "That is the day's goal met. We grew too, while you read. A good day's work for all four of us.",
            "Goal met. Bean wants to celebrate. Maize wants to rest. Squash says both, in that order.",
            "All your pages for today. A full basket. We know a full basket when we see one.",
